    {
      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_21e73332",
      "@type": "OverallIntent",
      "instance_name": "overallintent_instance",
      "label": "the overallintent",
      "description": "meme-id: when-your-stoner-friend-looks-in-your-fridge-goat-meme; hasOverallIntent: harmful; overall-intent-description: The meme depicts a goat staring directly at the viewer with a seemingly judgmental or mischievous expression, paired with the text 'when your stoner friend looks in your fridge.' The overall intent is to humorously portray the stereotypical behavior of a stoner friend who might be unexpectedly intrusive or chaotic when accessing another person's personal space (the fridge). The goat's expression is used as an analogical stand-in for the stoner friend's perceived 'weird' or 'unpredictable' demeanor. While the meme is lighthearted and relies on a common social joke, it could be considered harmful in that it reinforces a negative stereotype about stoners (implying they are irresponsible or intrusive), which may be offensive to some individuals or communities. The meme does not contain direct hate or abusive language, but it does rely on a potentially derogatory caricature of a social group, which can contribute to a broader culture of stereotyping and may be perceived as demeaning by those who identify with or are close to the stoner community. The humor is derived from the juxtaposition of the innocent-looking goat with the potentially chaotic human behavior described in the text, creating a comedic contrast.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
        "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#analysis_33daed2a"
      },
      "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface"
    },
